cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to the study it contains, please cite it
  using the metadata below. GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository"
  button.
title: >-
  Subsea Cable Routing & Data Centre Planning: an interactive planning tool and
  a controlled evaluation of least-cost-path cable routing
abstract: >-
  An interactive planning tool for submarine cable routing and data centre
  siting, and an original study testing the premise underlying least-cost-path
  cable route planners: that real cable positions are substantially explained by
  seabed terrain. Measured against 412 as-laid routes republished by seven
  national hydrographic offices, terrain preference is real but small, and a
  bathymetry-free alternative -- proximity to existing cables -- predicts real
  routes better and strengthens with route length.
type: software
